    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our premier play (80.98). Facing a favorable xERA of 4.80 from Ober, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill projection and, crucially, a slow delivery profile that significantly bolsters his stolen base upside\u2014our primary KPI. Following closely is **Christian Yelich** (74.22), whose lead-off spot against a right-handed matchup provides the optimal environment for high-volume scoring. **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) also grade out as strong starts; **Lars Nootbaar** in particular thrives today against a soft 5.29 xERA, while **Kazuma Okamoto** capitalizes on a high-upside platoon split that compensates for a neutral matchup profile.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (34.47), who ultimately missed the cut as he fell below our 40-point efficiency floor. While **Chase Meidroth** benefits from neutral park factors, his bottom-of-the-order positioning (Order #9) and a poor SP skill adjustment against Miles proved too heavy of a drag on his overall output. We are also monitoring the lower-ceiling outcomes for **Casey Schmitt** (42.63), who remains in the lineup despite a tough matchup against Miller, B, as his dynamic platoon advantage just barely keeps him above the threshold. We are holding **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Hyeseong Kim** on the bench due to off-days or minor league status, leaving the heavy lifting to our core group. We remain vigilant regarding the risk of high-tier arms like Miller, B, which could stifle production for **Casey Schmitt** and **Yordan Alvarez** (56.17) if they fail to capitalize on early-count opportunities.",
